# /etc/stayconnect/pmsd.env — the DARK environment for stayconnect-pmsd.service.
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF SETTINGS, and that is the whole point.
#
# `EnvironmentFile=` in the unit is not optional, so the file must exist or systemd refuses to start the
# service. What it must NOT do is carry configuration the dark daemon has no business having.
#
# With no STAYCONNECT_PHASE3_* variable set, iamv2.LoadPMSConfigFromEnv resolves every flag to OFF, and
# pmsd.Run returns immediately: no assignment is loaded, no database pool is constructed, no secret is
# decrypted, no worker starts and no PMS socket is opened. The process logs that it has nothing to do and
# exits 0. `Restart=on-failure` (not `always`) means a clean exit is a clean exit, so DARK never restart-loops.
#
# The flags are ABSENT rather than written as `=false` on purpose: the deployment gate proves darkness by
# asserting that no Phase-3 flag name appears in any env file or unit on the appliance, and a file that spells
# them out — even set to false — would weaken that proof into "somebody read the values correctly".
#
# TURNING THE CONNECTOR ON IS A SEPARATE, EXPLICITLY AUTHORIZED STEP. It needs, at minimum:
#
#   STAYCONNECT_PHASE3_MASTER=true            the master switch (a surface flag without it is a startup failure)
#   STAYCONNECT_PHASE3_PMS_CONNECTOR=true     and/or STAYCONNECT_PHASE3_PMS_INGEST=true
#   PMSD_DB_URL=...                           least-privilege DSN for the site database
#   PMSD_ASSIGNMENT_FILE=...                  signed assignment path
#   PMSD_ASSIGNMENT_PUBKEY_HEX=...            control-plane verification key
#   PMSD_SECRET_KEY_ID / PMSD_SECRET_KEY_HEX  interface-secret keyring
#   PMSD_EVIDENCE_KEY_HEX / ..._VERSION       evidence keys
#   PMSD_EVENT_IDENTITY_KEY_HEX / ..._VERSION event-identity keys
#
# None of those belongs here while Phase 3 is dark, and none of them is installed by
# scripts/install-pmsd-dark.sh.
